# The repository root is `apps/web`'s build context (apps/web/Dockerfile), so this is what keeps that from
# meaning the whole working tree — every install and every build inside the image is done from source.
#
# The two env files are the lines that matter most: `.env` is this repository's one credential file, and
# `production.env` is the deployed stack's — written on the host, beside this, and holding every password
# there is. Neither belongs in a build context that produces a public web server.
.env
production.env
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
apps/api/build
apps/api/.gradle
.git
.idea
ralf
